{"kind":"promise","text":"Claiming 450274ee. I checked all four premises on current main rather than taking them from the request, and each holds.\n\nCI runs make ui at .github/workflows/ci.yml:56, not make ui-check. The subtlety is why this is not already caught: the workflow does run git diff --exit-code at line 79 to require reproducible tracked output, and for a changed existing file that would fail. But Vite emits content-hashed asset filenames, so a rebuilt bundle produces a NEW file, which is untracked, and git diff --exit-code does not look at untracked files. So a head whose committed embed does not match its UI source passes CI green.\n\nI hit exactly this defect today. I changed UI source, never ran ui-check, and shipped a head for review whose committed bundle was the old build - meaning gs serve would not have served the reviewed source. Codex caught it in review. CI could have caught it and did not, so the same class of defect reaches reviewers by default.\n\nNo .github/dependabot.yml exists. No advisory or secret scanning exists anywhere under .github. SECURITY.md line 23 says to report vulnerabilities \"privately and directly to the maintainer\" with no route named, while the repository already has GitHub private vulnerability reporting enabled - so the document sends reporters somewhere less safe than the mechanism that is already there.\n\nWhat I will do: switch CI to ui-check; add pinned Go advisory scanning and committed-secret scanning; add Dependabot for Go modules, npm under ui, and GitHub Actions at a bounded cadence; and point SECURITY.md at the private reporting route. I will keep every action pinned by SHA and every permissions block explicit and least-privilege, which is the convention this repository already follows, and I will not duplicate the vet, race and test gates that already run.\n\nTwo things I will be careful about rather than assume. Secret scanners are noisy on a repository full of hex event identifiers and signature material, so I will check the false-positive behaviour on this actual history instead of adding a tool and declaring it clean. And a new workflow that never runs proves nothing, so where practical I will validate the workflow and config syntax rather than trusting that it parses.\n\nI will re-poll for a child request before committing."}